# Follow-up to 2026-10-02-23.play: the camera row visibly re-zooms the
# settings screen's own backdrop (FAR pulls the whole raid into view, FACE
# shrinks it to almost nothing behind the BACKDROP row). Next question: does
# the FACE extreme still let a real pull be played, or does it zoom in past
# the point a telegraph can be read?
#
# Two prior attempts in this same session both tried a second `open #hash`
# after the settings leg and landed back on `screen=home` with the hash
# silently ignored -- direction.md's own driver lesson (line 1579: a second
# `open #hash` in one script is a same-document fragment-navigation trap,
# `page.goto` to a hash-only URL does not reload the document, so
# `parseInvite`'s one-time read at module load never runs again). Worked
# around by never re-opening at all: normal in-app navigation (tap raid ->
# next -> classpick) is real SPA routing, not a `page.goto`, so it carries
# the zoom setting `saveZoom` already wrote to localStorage.

open
tap settings
tap camera:6
note camera set to FACE (closest), before entering a real pull
tap back

tap raid
targets
tap next
targets
tap class:mage:frost
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot face-opening
play idle 20
shot face-mid
state
